'''Orlando L. Watters''' (October 26, 1971 – June 8, 2026) was an American professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[cornerback]] for the [[Seattle Seahawks]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL) in 1994.{{refn|{{Cite web |title=Orlando Watters |url=https://www.nfl.com/players/orlando-watters/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20220530044720/https://www.nfl.com/players/orlando-watters/ |archive-date=2022-05-30 |access-date=2022-05-30 |website=[[National Football League]] |language=en-US}}}} He played [[college football]] for the [[Arkansas Razorbacks football|Arkansas Razorbacks]].{{refn|{{Cite news |last=Boling |first=Dave |date=1994-09-26 |title=Orlando's magic results in TD for rookie Watters |language=en-US |work=[[Kitsap Sun]] |url=https://products.kitsapsun.com/archive/1994/09-26/298494_orlando__39_s_magic_results_in_.html |url-status=live |access-date=2022-05-30 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20220530044144/https://products.kitsapsun.com/archive/1994/09-26/298494_orlando__39_s_magic_results_in_.html |archive-date=2022-05-30}}}} 

Watters died on June 8, 2026, at the age of 54.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jones |first1=Matt |title=Orlando Watters, Arkansas football star in early SEC years, dies at 54 |url=https://www.wholehogsports.com/news/2026/jun/09/orlando-watters-arkansas-football-star-in-early-sec-years-dies-at-54/ |access-date=10 June 2026 |publisher=Whole Hog Sports |date=9 June 2026}}</ref>
